{
  "slug": "claude-live-title",
  "name": "Claude Live Title",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Automatically generates meaningful session titles in real-time, replacing default random slugs (like \"elegant-chasing-eich\") with descriptive titles (like \"Fix pagination bug in API\").\n\nKey features:\n- Live updates: titles appear during conversation, not just after it ends\n- Multilingual: auto-detects conversation language, or set a preferred language manually\n- Smart throttling: first message triggers immediately, then rate-limited to save API calls\n- Non-blocking: all hooks run async, zero impact on your workflow\n- Configurable: model, language, throttle interval, title length — all adjustable via /claude-live-title:config\n- Works with Claude HUD: titles are displayed in the statusline when paired with claude-hud plugin\n- Cross-platform: Linux and macOS supported\n- Zero dependencies: only requires bash and jq (no npm, no pip)",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill** and **2 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `config` (Use when the user asks to \\\"view claude-live-title settings\\\", \\\"change title language\\\", \\\"configure live title\\\", \\\"adjust throttle interval\\\",…)\n- **Hooks** (2): `UserPromptSubmit`, `Stop`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install claude-live-title@claude-community` from `macworld/claude-live-title`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 1,
    "hook": 2
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
